# Normalise to LF in the repository *and* in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# index.js is the published `gemi` binary and opens with a shebang. Checked out
# through core.autocrlf=true on Windows it would gain CRLF, and `npm publish`
# from that clone ships "#!/usr/bin/env node\r" -- which Linux and macOS reject
# with "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env node^M".
#
# CI cannot catch this for us: the Unix runners check out LF whatever the
# author's setting, and the Windows job runs the bin through an npm-generated
# .cmd shim that never reads the shebang. So it is pinned here instead.
* text=auto eol=lf
